.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt LANDSTRIP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm landstrip
.Nd run commands inside an OS-level sandbox
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -debug
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sandboxes programs using JSON or YAML policies in a supported subset of the
Anthropic Sandbox Runtime format.
Use
.Nm Ar command Fl -help
for command help.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "policy validate"
.It Cm run
Run under the merged policy; the
.Fl -
separator before the program is required.
.It Cm policy validate
Check parsing, paths, executable policy, and platform support.
.It Cm policy resolve
Print the normalized merged policy as JSON.
.It Cm doctor
Report sandbox health.
.It Cm windows install
Install restricted-user isolation; requires elevation.
.It Cm windows prepare-appcontainer
Prepare null-device and root directory lookup access for standard AppContainer and LPAC;
requires elevation and verifies both modes without changing restricted users.
.It Cm windows status
Report the active implementation and its health.
.It Cm windows uninstall
Remove restricted-user isolation and return to AppContainer.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss General
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -debug
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help.
.El
.Ss Policy input
For
.Cm run , policy validate , policy resolve :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar file , Fl -policy Ar file
Read a policy; repeat to merge files.
Use
.Sq -
for stdin with
.Fl -policy-format .
.It Fl -policy-format Ar format
Select
.Va json
or
.Va yaml .
.It Fl -tool Ar program
Include the resolved executable's policy when validating or resolving.
.El
.Ss Run descriptors
Linux/macOS only; descriptors must be open, distinct, and numbered 3 or higher.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -trap Ar FD
Write events to one descriptor; not repeatable.
The program never inherits it.
Linux supports runtime broker traps and approval queries; macOS reports only
setup/launch failures and closes it on successful exec.
See
.Sx OUTPUT .
.It Fl -inherit Ar FD[,FD...]
Preserve a comma-separated descriptor list across exec; repeat to append.
Duplicates and overlap with
.Fl -trap
are rejected.
Inherited descriptors bypass pathname/network policy for their resources.
Other descriptors except stdin, stdout, and stderr are closed before exec.
.El
.Ss Windows installation
For
.Cm windows install :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -restricted-accounts Ar count
Set the restricted-network account pool size.
.It Fl -unrestricted-accounts Ar count
Set the unrestricted-network account pool size.
.It Fl -proxy-port-range Ar low-high
Set the restricted-user loopback proxy range.
.El
.Sh POLICY
Policies and their filesystem sections must be objects.
Objects merge recursively, arrays combine without duplicates, and later scalars
win; executable policy merges last.
Hard-denial roots
.Pq Va denyReadAlways No and Va denyWriteAlways
accumulate across documents, including newline-string lists;
empty/null values cannot clear earlier roots.
.Pp
Example fields, subject to the platform limits below:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "filesystem": {
    "allowWrite": ["."], "denyWrite": ["**/.env"],
    "denyWriteAlways": ["~/vault/secrets"],
    "denyRead": ["~/.ssh"], "allowRead": ["~/.ssh/config"],
    "denyReadAlways": ["~/.config/agent/auth.json"]
  },
  "network": {
    "allowNetwork": false, "allowLocalBinding": false,
    "httpProxyPort": 8080, "socksProxyPort": 8081,
    "allowUnixSockets": []
  },
  "windows": { "appContainerMode": "lpac", "allowLoopback": false }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Relative paths use the starting directory; tilde uses the current user's home.
Entries accept shell-style globs.
.Ss Filesystem
Writes default to denied.
.Va allowWrite
grants roots;
.Va denyWrite
takes precedence.
.Va denyWriteAlways
cannot be overridden by grants or broker approval.
Reads default to unrestricted on Linux/macOS.
.Va allowRead
adds exceptions to
.Va denyRead ,
but never
.Va denyReadAlways .
Protected roots and descendants stay denied through canonical symlink aliases
and broker approval.
Use concrete credential paths: read globs expand only at startup.
.Pp
Linux/macOS enforce concrete and glob write denials at access time;
Windows enforces only concrete paths existing at startup.
.Ss Network
Direct TCP is denied by default.
Linux/macOS proxy ports permit host-local TCP but do not start proxies.
.Va allowLocalBinding
permits host-local TCP/UDP binding and connections, not remote UDP.
Linux mediates per-datagram destinations and permits AF_UNSPEC disconnection.
macOS's localhost matcher may include other local interfaces, not just loopback.
.Va allowUnixSockets
permits listed pathname sockets, otherwise denied.
Windows supports neither local binding nor Unix socket policy.
.Va allowNetwork
permits general access, including remote UDP, without relaxing filesystem or
escape-prevention rules.
.Ss Windows
Requires explicit read grants and rejects nonempty
.Va denyReadAlways
and
.Va denyWriteAlways
before path resolution, even for missing paths or unmatched globs.
.Va windows.appContainerMode
selects
.Va lpac
(default, stronger) or
.Va standard .
.Va windows.allowLoopback
exposes all local loopback services in AppContainer mode, without per-port
proxy grants.
Restricted-user mode permits only the proxy range chosen at installation.
.Sh PLATFORM NOTES
.Bl -tag -width Windows
.It Linux
Landlock enforces filesystem roots; seccomp brokers network/filesystem traps
and blocks service-manager sockets even with unrestricted networking.
Linux 6.12+ also restricts abstract Unix sockets and signals outside
the sandbox.
io_uring setup/enter/register are blocked; an active
.Dv IORING_SETUP_SQPOLL
ring supplied by another process can consume shared-memory submissions outside
this boundary.
.It macOS
Seatbelt fixes the profile at startup.
.Dv AF_ROUTE
sockets remain available under every network policy for route/interface
discovery; kernel checks prevent unprivileged route changes.
.It Windows
AppContainer or restricted users enforce explicit filesystem grants;
restricted-user networking uses Windows Filtering Platform.
.Pp
If AppContainer cannot open
.Pa NUL ,
Git for Windows and shell null redirections fail regardless of policy.
Run
.Cm landstrip windows prepare-appcontainer
from an interactive Windows session after each reboot.
This repeatable, machine-wide change grants non-inheritable read/write access
to ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES and ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES.
Existing denies, ownership, and auditing are preserved.
It adds no sandbox filesystem/network policy grants or background service;
commands stay unelevated.
.Pp
In AppContainer mode,
.Cm doctor
and
.Cm windows status
probe fresh null-device and root directory lookup access with standard and LPAC tokens.
Setup/access failures produce unhealthy reports with mode-specific errors,
not certification that every tool or dependency can start.
Integration tests require null-device preparation and do not request elevation.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT
Policy, doctor, and Windows management commands write one JSON document
to stdout.
Failures and reported Linux broker denials are JSON lines on stderr with stable
.Va kind
and
.Va code
fields.
Kinds:
.Va filesystem , network , launch , usage , internal .
Filesystem/network events are Linux-only, not an exhaustive access audit.
.Pp
.Fl -trap
receives these events except usage errors.
Linux approval queries require a bidirectional stream socket and appear
only there.
Reply with a JSON line containing the unchanged string
.Va query_id
and
.Va action
of
.Dq allow
or
.Dq deny .
An unanswered query holds the syscall.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm run
returns the program's status.
With a Linux seccomp broker, remaining descendants
are terminated and reaped on exit; background processes cannot outlive the run.
Other failures, including invalid policies and unhealthy reports, return 1;
usage errors return 2.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
landstrip run -p policy.json -- cargo test
landstrip policy validate -p - --policy-format yaml < policy.yaml
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://github.com/landstrip/landstrip#readme
